coder › Implemented `Cache` in `src/cache.ts` and expanded `src/cache.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/cache.ts`
  - Backing store is a `Map<K, { value: V; expiresAt: number }>`, whose insertion order encodes recency.
  - `get` returns `undefined` for missing keys; expired entries are removed and returned as `undefined`; a live hit is re-inserted at the end of the map so it counts as a use.
  - `set` prunes expired entries, replaces an existing key's value/expiry in place (refreshing recency without evicting), and otherwise evicts the least-recently-used entry when the live size would exceed capacity.
  - `has` and `delete` treat expired entries as absent; `delete` returns `true` only when it removed a live entry.
  - `size` counts only non-expired entries.
  - The constructor throws `RangeError` when `!(capacity >= 1)` — this covers 0, negatives, and also `NaN`.
  - Expiry is `expiresAt = now() + ttlMs`, with an entry considered expired once `now() >= expiresAt`.

- `src/cache.test.ts`
  - Added 11 tests covering missing keys, expiry boundaries, set-replace-without-evicting, expiry refresh on set, LRU eviction via `get`, expired-entry pruning before eviction, `has`, `delete`, `size`, the default clock, and `RangeError` for capacity < 1.

